  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1250 PM CDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nTuesday is expected to be warm and breezy as the mid week storm\nsystem begins to impact the Plains. A corridor of widespread rains\nwill develop west of the region Tuesday night and spread slowly\neastward into the day Wednesday. Guidance has come into somewhat\nbetter agreement on timing for a renewed corridor of showers and\nstorms developing late Wednesday into Thursday across the local\nregion. Deep moisture plume from tropical remnant of Pollo will be\ningested into this storm system and expectations remain for heavy\nrainfall potential however the axis of heaviest rains remains\nuncertain. Wind fields will strengthen as the storm system\napproaches but instability will be tempered by the deep moist\nprofiles. These details will impact any severe weather potential\nand will also be refined in later forecasts. \n\nTiming of the upper trough to pass across the Plains has not yet\nbecome consistent with widely varying solutions still being shown.\nThe forecast will retain a low chance of rain into next weekend\nlargely a reflection of the timing uncertainty. Once the upper\ntrough does pass a cooler and drier airmass likely overspreads the\nregion.",
